1. MOTIVATION
1.1 Purpose and Task
This dataset was created to support Black Box Optimization (BBO) research, specifically to develop and evaluate Bayesian Optimization strategies for finding optimal input points without explicit knowledge of objective function structure or gradients.
1.2 Primary Research Questions
The dataset enables investigation of:
* How effectively can Gaussian Process (GP) surrogate models guide optimization across varying dimensionalities (2D to 8D)?
* Does the Upper Confidence Bound (UCB) acquisition function consistently find good solutions?
* How does optimization performance scale with problem dimensionality?
* Can iterative refinement with limited evaluations (1 per round) find near-optimal solutions?
1.3 Application Domain
This is a synthetic benchmark optimization problem, suitable for:
* Testing and validating optimization algorithms
* Educational demonstrations of Bayesian Optimization
* Benchmarking surrogate model quality
* Academic research in hyperparameter optimization and black-box optimization
1.4 Related Work
This project adapts established BBO benchmark functions from optimization literature to create a comprehensive test suite for evaluating Bayesian Optimization strategies in varying dimensionality.

